{
    "background_story": "Maria grew up during a time of economic hardship, where every penny counted. Her parents, immigrants who worked multiple jobs to make ends meet, instilled in her the value of frugality. As she grew older, Maria became known for her thrifty ways, always finding creative ways to stretch a dollar. She would repurpose old clothes, cook meals from scratch, and even repair broken appliances instead of replacing them. When she inherited a small plot of land from her grandmother, Maria turned it into a thriving garden, growing her own fruits and vegetables. Her thrifty nature allowed her to save enough money to start a small business, a second-hand store that became a staple in the community. Maria's motto, 'Use it up, wear it out, make it do, or do without,' inspired others to adopt a more frugal lifestyle.",
